  "note": "CR 702.180b's creature is chosen at CR 601.2b and tapped as the cost is paid; the two part company when the chosen creature is tapped for mana in CR 601.2g's window instead. One board, run twice: five Islands, Llanowar Elves and Bird Maiden (both power 1), Unending Whisper in alice's graveyard. The ChooseCost prompt shows the unreduced cost, then the harmonize candidate naming the Elves, then the Maiden's. Here alice names the Elves and taps them for {G}, so the payment has no untapped creature to tap and CR 734.1 reverses the whole cast, the mana abilities included: no card drawn, the Whisper still in the graveyard, and the Maiden untapped, which a tap pinned to a power rather than an object would have taken. The -control file names the Maiden on the same board with the same Elves tapped for mana, and the cast is paid. The mana never separates them: {5}{U} less one is {4}{U}, which the Elves and four Islands pay in both runs."
